      <Comment>In steryl esters, one acyl chain, denoted by R1, is connected to the sterol backbone via an ester linkage on the C3 carbon. For unsaturated acyl chains, the number, location, and orientation of the double bonds will vary between individual members of this group of compounds. The subclass is determined by the aryl chain on the backbone denotated by the R2 group.</Comment>
